        },
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "$y=-|x+2|$",
          "worked": "Replace $x$ by $-x$ in the equation from part (a).\n\n$$\\begin{align*} y&=-|-x-2|\\\\ y&=-|-(x+2)|\\\\ y&=-|x+2| \\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 10
      },
      {
        "id": "p5-p1-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "Repeat parts (a) and (b), but the other way around. Verify that you obtain the same result as part (b).",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": "Reflect across the $y$-axis to get $y=|x+2|$, then across the $x$-axis to get $y=-|x+2|$, as in part (b).",
          "worked": "For reflection across the $y$-axis, replace $x$ by $-x$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*} y&=|-x-2|\\\\ y&=|-(x+2)|\\\\ y&=|x+2| \\end{align*}$$\n\nReflection across the $x$-axis gives $y=-|x+2|$, the same equation as in part (b).",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 18
      }
    ]
